blocks.en:
Consider a system of linear equations
\begin{equation}\label{eq:holmgren-linear-first-order-system}
a_{ij}^k(\bm{x})\dfrac{\partial u_j}{\partial x_k}+b_{ij}(\bm{x})u_j=0,\qquad i=1,\ldots,N.
\end{equation}
Let $\bm{u}=(u_1,\ldots,u_N)$ be a solution in a "lens-shaped" domain $\Omega\subset\mathbb{R}^n$ bounded by two surfaces $S$ and $Z$. Assume that $\bm{u}=0$ on $Z$ and that $S$ is noncharacteristic and analytic. We also assume that the coefficients in \eqref{eq:holmgren-linear-first-order-system} are analytic.

blocks.zh:
考虑线性方程组
\begin{equation}\label{eq:holmgren-linear-first-order-system}
a_{ij}^k(\bm{x})\dfrac{\partial u_j}{\partial x_k}+b_{ij}(\bm{x})u_j=0,\qquad i=1,\ldots,N.
\end{equation}
设 $\bm{u}=(u_1,\ldots,u_N)$ 是由两个曲面 $S$ 和 $Z$ 围成的"透镜形"区域 $\Omega\subset\mathbb{R}^n$ 内的解. 假设在 $Z$ 上 $\bm{u}=0$, 且 $S$ 非特征并解析. 还假设 \eqref{eq:holmgren-linear-first-order-system} 中的系数解析.

blocks.en:
Let $v_i$, $i=1,\ldots,N$ be arbitrary functions in $C^1(\overline\Omega)$. We multiply the $i$th equation of \eqref{eq:holmgren-linear-first-order-system} by $v_i$, sum over $i$, and integrate over $\Omega$. This yields
\begin{equation}\label{eq:holmgren-integration-by-parts}
\begin{aligned}
0&=\int_\Omega v_i(\bm{x})a_{ij}^k(\bm{x})\dfrac{\partial u_j}{\partial x_k}(\bm{x})+
v_i(\bm{x})b_{ij}(\bm{x})u_j(\bm{x})\,\mathrm{d}\bm{x}\\
&=\int_\Omega-\dfrac{\partial}{\partial x_k}[v_i(\bm{x})a_{ij}^k(\bm{x})]u_j(\bm{x})
+v_i(\bm{x})b_{ij}(\bm{x})u_j(\bm{x})\,\mathrm{d}\bm{x}\\
&\quad+\int_{\partial\Omega}a_{ij}^k(\bm{x})v_i(\bm{x})u_j(\bm{x})n_k\,\mathrm{d}S,
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
where $\bm{n}$ is the outer normal to $\partial\Omega$.

blocks.zh:
令 $v_i$, $i=1,\ldots,N$ 为 $C^1(\overline\Omega)$ 中的任意函数. 将 \eqref{eq:holmgren-linear-first-order-system} 的第 $i$ 个方程乘以 $v_i$, 对 $i$ 求和, 并在 $\Omega$ 上积分, 得到
\begin{equation}\label{eq:holmgren-integration-by-parts}
\begin{aligned}
0&=\int_\Omega v_i(\bm{x})a_{ij}^k(\bm{x})\dfrac{\partial u_j}{\partial x_k}(\bm{x})+
v_i(\bm{x})b_{ij}(\bm{x})u_j(\bm{x})\,\mathrm{d}\bm{x}\\
&=\int_\Omega-\dfrac{\partial}{\partial x_k}[v_i(\bm{x})a_{ij}^k(\bm{x})]u_j(\bm{x})
+v_i(\bm{x})b_{ij}(\bm{x})u_j(\bm{x})\,\mathrm{d}\bm{x}\\
&\quad+\int_{\partial\Omega}a_{ij}^k(\bm{x})v_i(\bm{x})u_j(\bm{x})n_k\,\mathrm{d}S,
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
其中 $\bm{n}$ 为 $\partial\Omega$ 的外法向量.

blocks.en:
Assume now that $\bm{v}$ satisfies the "adjoint" system of PDEs,
\begin{equation}\label{eq:holmgren-adjoint-system}
-\dfrac{\partial}{\partial x_k}(a_{ij}^kv_i)+b_{ij}v_i=0,\qquad j=1,\ldots,N,
\end{equation}
with initial conditions
\begin{equation}\label{eq:holmgren-adjoint-cauchy-data}
v_i=f_i
\end{equation}
on $S$. Then \eqref{eq:holmgren-integration-by-parts} reduces to
\begin{equation}\label{eq:holmgren-boundary-pairing}
0=\int_Sa_{ij}^k(\bm{x})f_i(\bm{x})u_j(\bm{x})n_k\,\mathrm{d}S.
\end{equation}

blocks.zh:
现在假设 $\bm{v}$ 满足"伴随"偏微分方程组
\begin{equation}\label{eq:holmgren-adjoint-system}
-\dfrac{\partial}{\partial x_k}(a_{ij}^kv_i)+b_{ij}v_i=0,\qquad j=1,\ldots,N,
\end{equation}
及 $S$ 上的初始条件
\begin{equation}\label{eq:holmgren-adjoint-cauchy-data}
v_i=f_i
\end{equation}
则 \eqref{eq:holmgren-integration-by-parts} 化为
\begin{equation}\label{eq:holmgren-boundary-pairing}
0=\int_Sa_{ij}^k(\bm{x})f_i(\bm{x})u_j(\bm{x})n_k\,\mathrm{d}S.
\end{equation}

blocks.en:
\begin{enumerate}
\item The set $\bigcup_{\lambda\in[a,b]}S_\lambda$ is compact.
\item $S_a$ consists of a single point located on $Z$.
\item For $a<\lambda<b$, $S_\lambda$ is a regular surface intersecting $Z$ transversally (the intersection of two surfaces is called transverse if their normals are not collinear). The intersection of $S_\lambda$ and $Z$ is then a regular (analytic) $(n-2)$-dimensional surface. Moreover, we assume that $S_\lambda$ is noncharacteristic.
\end{enumerate}

blocks.zh:
\begin{enumerate}
\item 集合 $\bigcup_{\lambda\in[a,b]}S_\lambda$ 是紧的.
\item $S_a$ 由位于 $Z$ 上的一个点构成.
\item 对 $a<\lambda<b$, $S_\lambda$ 为与 $Z$ 横截相交的正则曲面 (若两个曲面的法向量不共线, 就称其相交为横截相交). 此时 $S_\lambda$ 与 $Z$ 的交是一个正则 (解析) 的 $(n-2)$ 维曲面. 此外, 假设 $S_\lambda$ 非特征.
\end{enumerate}

blocks.en:
Consider the wave equation in two dimensions
\begin{equation}\label{eq:wave-determinacy-example}
u_{yy}-u_{xx}=0,
\end{equation}
with Cauchy data prescribed for $y=0$, $-1<x<1$. Let $\Phi(x,y)=(x-y+1)(x+y-1)$, and let $D=(-1,1)\times(-1,1)$. Then $S_\lambda$, $-1\leq\lambda<0$ is the arc of the hyperbola $(x-y+1)(x+y-1)=\lambda$ that lies within the triangle with corners $(-1,0)$, $(1,0)$ and $(0,1)$. It is easy to show that all the hypotheses of the theorem are satisfied with $a=-1$ and any $b\in(-1,0)$. Since the $S_\lambda$ fill the interior of the triangle, $u$ is determined within the whole triangle by its prescribed Cauchy data. In general, if $u$ is determined in $\Omega$ by its Cauchy data on $Z$, we call $\Omega$ a \emph{domain of determinacy} for $Z$.

blocks.zh:
考虑二维波动方程
\begin{equation}\label{eq:wave-determinacy-example}
u_{yy}-u_{xx}=0,
\end{equation}
在 $y=0$, $-1<x<1$ 上给定 Cauchy 数据. 令 $\Phi(x,y)=(x-y+1)(x+y-1)$, 并令 $D=(-1,1)\times(-1,1)$. 那么对 $-1\leq\lambda<0$, $S_\lambda$ 是双曲线 $(x-y+1)(x+y-1)=\lambda$ 位于顶点为 $(-1,0)$, $(1,0)$ 和 $(0,1)$ 的三角形内部的弧. 容易证明, 取 $a=-1$ 及任意 $b\in(-1,0)$, 定理的所有假设都满足. 由于各个 $S_\lambda$ 填满三角形内部, 给定的 Cauchy 数据确定了整个三角形内的 $u$. 一般地, 若 $Z$ 上的 Cauchy 数据确定了 $\Omega$ 内的 $u$, 则称 $\Omega$ 为 $Z$ 的一个\emph{决定域}.

blocks.en:
First, we define
\begin{equation}\label{eq:weierstrass-kernel-integrals}
I_m=\int_0^1(1-v^2)^m\,\mathrm{d}v,\qquad I_{m,\delta}=\int_\delta^1(1-v^2)^m\,\mathrm{d}v.
\end{equation}
From the elementary inequalities
\begin{equation}\label{eq:weierstrass-kernel-integral-bounds}
I_m>\int_0^1(1-v)^m\,\mathrm{d}v=\dfrac1{m+1},\qquad I_{m,\delta}<(1-\delta^2)^m,
\end{equation}
we conclude that, for any positive $\delta$,
\begin{equation}\label{eq:weierstrass-kernel-tail-limit}
\lim_{m\to\infty}\dfrac{I_{m,\delta}}{I_m}=0.
\end{equation}

blocks.zh:
首先定义
\begin{equation}\label{eq:weierstrass-kernel-integrals}
I_m=\int_0^1(1-v^2)^m\,\mathrm{d}v,\qquad I_{m,\delta}=\int_\delta^1(1-v^2)^m\,\mathrm{d}v.
\end{equation}
从初等不等式
\begin{equation}\label{eq:weierstrass-kernel-integral-bounds}
I_m>\int_0^1(1-v)^m\,\mathrm{d}v=\dfrac1{m+1},\qquad I_{m,\delta}<(1-\delta^2)^m,
\end{equation}
得到对任意正的 $\delta$ 都有
\begin{equation}\label{eq:weierstrass-kernel-tail-limit}
\lim_{m\to\infty}\dfrac{I_{m,\delta}}{I_m}=0.
\end{equation}

blocks.en:
We now choose $\alpha$ and $\beta$ such that $0<\alpha<a<b<\beta<1$. We set
\begin{equation}\label{eq:weierstrass-one-dimensional-polynomial}
p_m(x)=\dfrac{\int_\alpha^\beta f(y)[1-(y-x)^2]^m\,\mathrm{d}y}{\int_{-1}^1(1-y^2)^m\,\mathrm{d}y}.
\end{equation}
Obviously, $p_m$ is a polynomial of degree $2m$. We shall now show that $p_m$ converges to $f$, uniformly on $[a,b]$. In the numerator, we set $y=v+x$, and obtain
\begin{equation}\label{eq:weierstrass-three-integral-split}
\begin{aligned}
\int_{\alpha-x}^{\beta-x}f(v+x)(1-v^2)^m\,\mathrm{d}v
&=\int_{\alpha-x}^{-\delta}\cdots+\int_{-\delta}^{\delta}\cdots+\int_\delta^{\beta-x}\cdots\\
&=I_1+I_2+I_3.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}

blocks.zh:
现在选取 $\alpha$ 和 $\beta$, 使得 $0<\alpha<a<b<\beta<1$. 令
\begin{equation}\label{eq:weierstrass-one-dimensional-polynomial}
p_m(x)=\dfrac{\int_\alpha^\beta f(y)[1-(y-x)^2]^m\,\mathrm{d}y}{\int_{-1}^1(1-y^2)^m\,\mathrm{d}y}.
\end{equation}
显然, $p_m$ 是次数为 $2m$ 的多项式. 下面证明 $p_m$ 在 $[a,b]$ 上一致收敛到 $f$. 在分子中令 $y=v+x$, 得到
\begin{equation}\label{eq:weierstrass-three-integral-split}
\begin{aligned}
\int_{\alpha-x}^{\beta-x}f(v+x)(1-v^2)^m\,\mathrm{d}v
&=\int_{\alpha-x}^{-\delta}\cdots+\int_{-\delta}^{\delta}\cdots+\int_\delta^{\beta-x}\cdots\\
&=I_1+I_2+I_3.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}

blocks.en:
Evidently, $|I_1|$ and $|I_3|$ are bounded by $MI_{m,\delta}$, where $M$ is the maximum of $|f|$. Let now $\epsilon>0$ be given and choose $\delta$ such that $|f(v+x)-f(x)|\leq\epsilon$ for $|v|\leq\delta$. Then we compute
\begin{equation}\label{eq:weierstrass-central-integral}
\begin{aligned}
I_2&=f(x)\int_{-\delta}^{\delta}(1-v^2)^m\,\mathrm{d}v\\
&\quad+\int_{-\delta}^{\delta}(f(x+v)-f(x))(1-v^2)^m\,\mathrm{d}v.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
The first term on the right equals $2f(x)(I_m-I_{m,\delta})$, and the second term can be estimated by $2\epsilon I_m$. By combining the estimates obtained, we find
\begin{equation}\label{eq:weierstrass-uniform-error-estimate}
|p_m(x)-f(x)|\leq2M\dfrac{I_{m,\delta}}{I_m}+\epsilon.
\end{equation}

blocks.zh:
显然, $|I_1|$ 和 $|I_3|$ 都以 $MI_{m,\delta}$ 为界, 其中 $M$ 为 $|f|$ 的最大值. 现在给定 $\epsilon>0$, 选取 $\delta$, 使得当 $|v|\leq\delta$ 时有 $|f(v+x)-f(x)|\leq\epsilon$. 计算得到
\begin{equation}\label{eq:weierstrass-central-integral}
\begin{aligned}
I_2&=f(x)\int_{-\delta}^{\delta}(1-v^2)^m\,\mathrm{d}v\\
&\quad+\int_{-\delta}^{\delta}(f(x+v)-f(x))(1-v^2)^m\,\mathrm{d}v.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
右端第一项等于 $2f(x)(I_m-I_{m,\delta})$, 第二项可用 $2\epsilon I_m$ 估计. 合并所得估计, 得到
\begin{equation}\label{eq:weierstrass-uniform-error-estimate}
|p_m(x)-f(x)|\leq2M\dfrac{I_{m,\delta}}{I_m}+\epsilon.
\end{equation}

blocks.en:
We can make this quantity as small as we wish by first choosing $\epsilon$ small, then choosing $\delta$ accordingly and then choosing $m$ sufficiently large.

In several space dimensions, we proceed in an analogous fashion with
\begin{equation}\label{eq:weierstrass-multivariable-polynomial}
p_m(\bm{x})=\dfrac{\int_{\alpha_1}^{\beta_1}\cdots\int_{\alpha_n}^{\beta_n}f(\bm{y})[1-(y_1-x_1)^2]^m\cdots[1-(y_n-x_n)^2]^m\,\mathrm{d}y_n\cdots\mathrm{d}y_1}{\left[\int_{-1}^1(1-\xi^2)^m\,\mathrm{d}\xi\right]^n}.
\end{equation}
\end{Proof}

blocks.zh:
先将 $\epsilon$ 取得很小, 再相应地选取 $\delta$, 最后将 $m$ 取得充分大, 就可使这个量任意小.

在多维空间中, 类似地使用
\begin{equation}\label{eq:weierstrass-multivariable-polynomial}
p_m(\bm{x})=\dfrac{\int_{\alpha_1}^{\beta_1}\cdots\int_{\alpha_n}^{\beta_n}f(\bm{y})[1-(y_1-x_1)^2]^m\cdots[1-(y_n-x_n)^2]^m\,\mathrm{d}y_n\cdots\mathrm{d}y_1}{\left[\int_{-1}^1(1-\xi^2)^m\,\mathrm{d}\xi\right]^n}.
\end{equation}
\end{Proof}

blocks.en:
Verify that
\begin{equation}\label{eq:flat-in-time-heat-series}
u(x,t)=\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}\dfrac{x^{2m}}{(2m)!}\dfrac{\mathrm{d}^m}{\mathrm{d}t^m}\exp\left(\dfrac{-1}{t^2}\right)
\end{equation}
is a solution of $u_t=u_{xx}$ with initial condition $u(x,0)=0$. Why does Holmgren's theorem not apply? Hint: Use Cauchy's formula to estimate derivatives of $\exp(-1/t^2)$. For the contour, choose a circle centered at $t$ with radius $t/2$.

blocks.zh:
验证
\begin{equation}\label{eq:flat-in-time-heat-series}
u(x,t)=\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}\dfrac{x^{2m}}{(2m)!}\dfrac{\mathrm{d}^m}{\mathrm{d}t^m}\exp\left(\dfrac{-1}{t^2}\right)
\end{equation}
是 $u_t=u_{xx}$ 满足初始条件 $u(x,0)=0$ 的一个解. 为什么不能应用 Holmgren 定理? Hint: 用 Cauchy 公式估计 $\exp(-1/t^2)$ 的导数. 积分路径选取以 $t$ 为中心, 半径为 $t/2$ 的圆周.
